+# Bounded official marketing check · 21 October 2026
+
+The prototype already uses genuine stored product captures for Glassdays and Mute On Location. Their public App Store identities were reconfirmed through primary pages:
+
+- [Glassdays, developer David Holtschke](https://apps.apple.com/de/app/countdown-glassdays/id6785538729).
+- [Mute On Location, developer David Holtschke](https://apps.apple.com/za/app/mute-on-location/id6790398791?mt=12). The first German URL could not be fetched by the web tool; the official regional result resolves the same numeric app ID.
+- [David Holtschke’s official App Store developer page](https://apps.apple.com/us/developer/david-holtschke/id6785538731?platform=iphone) lists Glassdays and Mute On Location. No NotiLog listing was found there or in bounded exact-name/developer App Store searches. This does not prove global absence; it provides no verified official screenshot to adopt.
+- The live [owner website](https://holtsdav.com/) has NotiLog text but its App Store label is not a link, unlike the two published apps. It supplies no product capture.
+
+The NotiLog repository’s image inventory contains its genuine light/dark app icons and three setup-step JPEGs. The latter are onboarding instructions rather than a full NotiLog product presentation. Its README describes release preparation, not a public listing. No invented App Store link or publication claim was added. NotiLog remains an intentional compact icon-led project page with useful verified facts.
+
+The Glassdays listing explicitly identifies its icon as an adaptation of Hourglass Bold from Solar Icon Set by 480 Design under CC BY 4.0. A linked attribution and adaptation notice was added to About. No public customer review, rating, price, revenue or testimonial was copied into the portfolio.
+
+No new marketing bitmap was necessary for the two apps already represented with genuine stored captures. No synthetic native-review screenshot was used, no native app was launched, and no native source was edited. **WorktreeLens and Fehlerblatt are not included** in the ten-project data file.
